From bcda915fe0a18f1ac8182c65351dd5fc1e54e2b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:19:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/18] Sign-in recovery, display reads by value, payment
 waits, shell fixes from the full-site review

- auth: an idle client whose session became unknown (wallet pick, account switch, 401 house check, failed or
  rate-limited session read) re-reads it itself with backoff; buttons no longer stay disabled until a reload.
  A locally expired session (W-1) stays quiet as designed. Reverts the earlier "keep the session object" change,
  which conflicted with the rule that a fresh read stays distinguishable.
- Display readers (GOLD ledger, wallet balances, Celestao order state) compare the session by wallet and expiry
  (sameSession); transaction and debit authority keep the strict identity check (tests require it).
- Payments: wait about 2 minutes for a receipt instead of 12 s; awaiting-credit text says it usually takes ~15 minutes;
  AUTH_REQUIRED wording covers a locked or unconnected wallet.
- HUD and GOLD panel: focus + visibilitychange make one read; HUD polls every 60 s.
- Shell: the interior no longer goes blank after closing Inventory opened inside the house; Esc closes the Map;
  closing GOLD/Economy drops ?portal=; Esc in the GOLD panel no longer also cancels a ride boarding.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
